API-16: refuse option values that an input file cannot hold

EN_setoption accepted values that saveinpfile cannot write in a form the
parser reads back. CHECKFREQ and MAXCHECK below 1 were truncated to 0,
which the parser refuses (error 213). The parser reads a VISCOSITY of
0.001 or less, and a DIFFUSIVITY of 0.0001 or less other than 0, as an
absolute value rather than one relative to water or chlorine, so such
relative values came back thousands of times too large, or as 0 and an
error. Refuse these values with 213, as EN_TRIALS does below 1.

Apply from the root of an EPANET checkout at 83e25bb:
    git apply API-16_fix.patch

diff --git a/src/epanet.c b/src/epanet.c
index 47dc1e4..36e1896 100644
--- a/src/epanet.c
+++ b/src/epanet.c
@@ -1371,15 +1371,19 @@ int DLLEXPORT EN_setoption(EN_Project p, int option, double value)
         break;
 
     case EN_SP_VISCOS:
-        if (value <= 0.0) return 213;
+        // An input file reads a VISCOSITY of 0.001 or less as an actual
+        // viscosity, so such relative values could not be saved
+        if (value <= 1.e-3) return 213;
         hyd->Viscos = value * VISCOS;
         break;
 
     case EN_CHECKFREQ:
+        if (value < 1.0) return 213;
         hyd->CheckFreq = (int)value;
         break;
 
     case EN_MAXCHECK:
+        if (value < 1.0) return 213;
         hyd->MaxCheck = (int)value;
         break;
 
@@ -1388,6 +1392,9 @@ int DLLEXPORT EN_setoption(EN_Project p, int option, double value)
         break;
 
     case EN_SP_DIFFUS:
+        // An input file reads a DIFFUSIVITY of 0.0001 or less (other than 0)
+        // as an actual diffusivity, so such relative values could not be saved
+        if (value > 0.0 && value <= 1.e-4) return 213;
         qual->Diffus = value * DIFFUS;
         break;
 
